#!/usr/bin/env bash
# SessionStart hook for knowledge-principles. Runs on every session start (Claude Code
# lifecycle) and injects the ten rules as ONE-LINE POINTERS plus the gate that decides
# which of them are active. It does NOT dump the rule skills: each rule carries its
# obligations, its violation symptoms and — critically — its "does not claim" limits in
# its own skill, which the model loads on demand via the Skill tool.
set -euo pipefail

python3 - <<'PY'
import json

reminder = (
    "<EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT>\n"
    "This environment ships the **knowledge-principles** rules: ten hard programming rules. "
    "A violation is a defect, not a preference.\n\n"
    "PRECEDENCE, before any rule: a codified project convention (a `knowledge-*` convention "
    "or the project's own CLAUDE.md) beats a framework idiom, which beats a universal "
    "principle. A mandated wrapper, factory or registry is compliance, not excess — never "
    "report one as a principle violation.\n\n"
    "PROPORTIONALITY, decide this FIRST, first match wins:\n"
    "  (a) does the change add or alter an endpoint, route, migration, schema, auth/session "
    "path, money path, or a package's public export? -> LEVEL 3\n"
    "  (b) does it live inside an existing application's source tree? -> LEVEL 2\n"
    "  (c) otherwise (scratch script, spike, throwaway helper) -> LEVEL 1\n"
    "Level is decided by WHAT KIND OF CODE, never by diff size. At level 1 only rules 1, 7, "
    "9 and 10 are active; at level 2 all ten; at level 3 all ten with 5 and 9 applied "
    "strictly. Rule 9 is a floor: active at every level, never overridden by any convention "
    "or idiom.\n\n"
    "THE TEN RULES (pointers, not the rules themselves):\n"
    "  1 clarity           — clarity over cleverness\n"
    "  2 abstraction       — I/O boundaries abstract immediately; domain abstracts on the "
    "third real case\n"
    "  3 boy-scout         — clean up touched lines only\n"
    "  4 module-boundaries — depend on the contract, not the structure\n"
    "  5 errors            — strict at input, fail fast inside, degrade at output\n"
    "  6 state             — single source of truth; never mutate what you do not own; "
    "illegal states unrepresentable\n"
    "  7 naming            — name the intent; make effects and dependencies explicit\n"
    "  8 performance       — known slow patterns are defects; optimisation requires "
    "measurement\n"
    "  9 security          — security by default\n"
    " 10 change-safety     — do not touch what you do not understand; observable behaviour "
    "is someone's dependency\n\n"
    "For anything beyond a trivial edit, invoke the `knowledge-principles:principles` skill "
    "(via the Skill tool) and read the rule that owns the question. These one-liners are "
    "pointers: a rule quoted without its \"does not claim\" limits is routinely applied "
    "where it does not reach. Where two rules genuinely collide, the umbrella skill's "
    "conflict table decides; where nothing decides, name the conflict and let the user "
    "choose — never resolve it silently.\n"
    "</EXTREMELY_IMPORTANT>"
)

print(json.dumps({
    "hookSpecificOutput": {
        "hookEventName": "SessionStart",
        "additionalContext": reminder,
    }
}))
PY
